  "description": "MAJDIP crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C90 H126 Br6 Gd6 N6 O42,5(C2 H3 N1),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.813-3.823 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.73-111.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C100H149Br6Gd6N11O43.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
